Z||000000||84fierotrevor||11-03-2001||03:29 PM||||I see those things on ebay for like 100 bucks ! and like 28 people bid on them !<BR>whats so great about them ? are they better then the normal fiero side scoop thingy ?<BR>does it add horse power ?<BR>why all the madness ?<P>------------------<BR>84 fiero 2m4 <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar_6.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-03-2001||03:40 PM||||The great thing is that they say "Holley" on the side of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually the only way they work better than the stock ones is if you remove the air box inside the wheel well and add a custom tube to the intake.  Do a search on custom air intakes and you will see  what all the madness is about.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||11-03-2001||03:42 PM||||I think it's a bunch of bull-pucky.  The stock intake works fine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||84fierotrevor||11-03-2001||03:44 PM||||im gonna paint the words holley on my scop then lol||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bazooka||11-03-2001||03:46 PM||||Style endorsed by a major name (Holley). It allows air to squeek thru a half dollar size opening just like the original, and doesn't do anything for a HP increase. Supply and Demand has raised the price because Holley doesn't make these any more. I have seen other people fabricating these on the net and they look very close to Holleys'.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||11-03-2001||03:50 PM||||That may be true on a stock engine, but when you've got a conversion (especially a V8) you want as much fresh air to get to the filter as possible.  My intake filter sits right inside the wheel well about 1/2" away from the "Holley" scoop.||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||11-03-2001||03:56 PM||||     I want to buy one just because I think they look cool. What websites can I find the remanufactured ones on?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||11-03-2001||04:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>I think it's a bunch of bull-pucky.  The stock intake works fine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I totally agree. I mean, what amount of horsepower increase are you gonna see anyways? Seriously!<P>Is 5hp worth the expense and tremendous amount of work/fabrication?<P>Geeeezzzz!!!!<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000008||AL||11-03-2001||05:08 PM||||it really doesn't increase horse power,but it looks better then the stock or the knock off holley scoop,i was lucky, i found one at the yard for 5 bucks,but i wouldn't pay 100 bucks for it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Old Lar||11-03-2001||08:04 PM||||The best thing about the Holley Side scoop, I mean the really best thing is having one and selling it to some fool for $100 and telling them that it will increase horsepower some phenomenal amount and having the fool believe it and happily parting with his money. As PT Barnum said "There is a sucker born every minute"||||reg||1
